---
title: Pad thai
servings: 2
tags: [chicken, stir-fry, quick]
cuisine: thai
time: 30 minutes
source: Pad Thai by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/chicken-pad-thai/
---

== Noodles ==

Cover the @rice noodles{125%g}(dried, pad thai width) with boiling water and
leave ~{5%minutes}. Drain, rinse briefly under cold water, and use within
10 minutes.

== Sauce ==

Stir together the @tamarind paste{1 1/2%tbsp}(puree, not concentrate),
@brown sugar{3%tbsp}(packed), @fish sauce{2%tbsp} and @oyster sauce{1 1/2%tbsp}.

== Stir-fry ==

Heat 2 tbsp of the @vegetable oil{2-3%tbsp} in a large #nonstick skillet{} over
high heat. Add the @yellow onion{1/2}(sliced) and @garlic{2%cloves}(finely chopped)
and stir ~{30%seconds}.

Add the @chicken{150%g}(breast or thigh, thinly sliced) and cook
~{1 1/2%minutes}, until nearly done.

Push the chicken aside, pour the @eggs{2}(lightly beaten) into the space, and
scramble them, adding the last of the oil if the pan is dry. Stir the egg
through the chicken.

Add the @bean sprouts{1 1/2%cups}, @tofu{1/2%cup}(firm, cut into 3 cm batons),
the noodles and the sauce. Toss gently ~{1 1/2%minutes}, until the noodles have
soaked up the sauce.

Toss in the @garlic chives{1/4%cup}(cut into 3 cm lengths) and half the
@roasted peanuts{1/4%cup}(finely chopped), then take it off the heat.

Serve straight away with the rest of the peanuts on top, and @lime{}(wedges),
@?cayenne pepper{} and more @bean sprouts{} on the side.

> Have everything cut and measured before the pan goes on; the whole stir-fry
> takes about five minutes.
